{%- comment -%}
  Emits an absolute URL, for JSON-LD and anywhere else a consumer outside the
  browser has to resolve the link without a base.

  Accepts: url (required)

  Three shapes reach this snippet:
    //cdn.shopify.com/...   image_url and asset_url are protocol-relative
    /products/wadi-rum      Liquid route and object URLs are site-relative
    https://...             already absolute; passed through untouched

  Liquid has no startswith, so the prefix is read with `slice`. Checking the
  two-character prefix first matters: every protocol-relative URL also starts
  with a single slash.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign scheme = url | slice: 0, 2
  assign leading = url | slice: 0, 1

  if scheme == '//'
    assign absolute = url | prepend: 'https:'
  elsif leading == '/'
    assign absolute = url | prepend: shop.url
  else
    assign absolute = url
  endif
-%}
{{- absolute -}}
